    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIt'd be nice to have a lua version of https://github.com/AndrewRadev/sideways.vim and it seems like it may fit well with mini.nvim. I haven't looked deeply, but it seems like TS would allow for a cleaner implementation, though I suspect TS won't cover everything. I particularly find the 'Adding items' feature useful for frontend development, where it's common to append properties as the last argument using the dot operator.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if you'd consider the `ai` module to be a good fit but there is some overlap since Sideways.vim also features text objects.\r\n\r\n",
