            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nI've used 'sideways.vim' myself up until 'mini.ai' with its argument textobject. I mostly used it for swapping arguments and replaced it with custom mapping using [tommcdo/vim-exchange](https://github.com/tommcdo/vim-exchange):\r\n- `<Cmd>normal cxiacxila<CR>` to move argument to the left.\r\n- `<Cmd>normal cxiacxina<CR>` to move argument to the right.\r\n\r\nThese are not ideal, but do the job.\r\n\r\nSo instead I am planning to implement 'mini.swap' (or 'mini.exchange') which will allow exchanging to text regions.",
